WEBVTT

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.350
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.730
<i>Nadia was captured by a mysterious organization named Neo Atlantis.</i>

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.860
<i>The masked leader who calls himself Gargoyle</i>

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.820
<i>demanded the Blue Water possessed by Nadia.</i>

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.570
<i>Under Gargoyle's inhuman questioning, Nadia disclosed</i>

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.410
<i>that Jean has the Blue Water in his possession.</i>

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.750
<i>Jean and Grandis's gang are hiding in the Tower of Babel,</i>

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.210
<i>an incredibly destructive weapon.</i>

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:52.250
<i>Testing of the Tower of Babel commenced before their eyes.</i>

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.670
<i>Its unbelievable power destroyed an entire island.</i>

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.470
<i>Resurrected now, Satan's Light is a force that can destroy the world.</i>

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.440
Captain Nemo!

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.740
We've traced the source of the killer beam. Direction SP03, RP40.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.330
Good. Full speed ahead to the source's position.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.080
Roger!

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.700
Main engines at maximum speed. Prepare to submerge.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.960
All personnel to general quarters.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.000
Roger.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.170
Both engine set to maximum speed. Prepare to submerge.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.590
Forward tanks, taking in water.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.260
Engine operation normal. Connecting to propulsion system.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.010
All ballast tanks filled, Sir.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.100
Commencing dive.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.770
Everything normal and steady, Sir.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.610
The Nautilus has reached her target depth.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.070
Return ship to level position.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.280
That fiend Gargoyle has finally completed his weapon,

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.950
his artificial Orihalcon and the Tower of Babel!

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.420
Wonderful!

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:25.680
With the Tower of Babel, our Atlantis will again rule the world.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.480
Pressure inside the Tower has returned to normal.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.940
Power generation and transmission systems are operating normally.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.770
Electron accelerator is normal.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.990
All memory devices are normal.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.610
All systems functioning normally, Sir.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.450
Good. Reset the test circuits.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:46.990
Yes, Sir!

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.540
Reset test circuits.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.000
Resetting test circuits.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.020
That was a horrible experience!

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.070
Are you okay, Hanson?

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.150
I guess so. What was that?

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.150
It appeared that a beam of light shot out.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.950
Right, like a bolt of lightning.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.160
Got you!

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:31.080
Hey kid, where's that girl?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:31.830
Now...

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.290
My child, tell me where the Blue Water is?

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.210
Nadia has been captured by them.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:42.630
What did you say?

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.390
Now that we have completed the Tower of Babel,

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.470
the only problem is Nemo and his Nautilus.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:54.850
You're my valuable guest until I can sink that submarine.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.480
You're a stubborn child, but

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:05.490
remember that the lives of Marie and the lion depend on how you act.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:11.870
And another thing. You'll see your boyfriend again real soon,

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.830
but he may be dead by now.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.840
Say, Miss...

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.430
What do we do now?

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.140
All right, Jean, why don't we join forces?

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:37.900
One for all and all for one.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.230
But...

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.610
You don't have to worry.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.110
We'll be partners until we leave this island.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:51.280
We'll keep our hands off the Blue Water that Nadia has, okay?

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.580
But maybe Nadia doesn't have it anymore.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.790
Then we'll just take it back from Gargoyle, right?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.920
Everything is settled. Let's get on with our act!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:02.840
Let's go, everyone!

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.260
Right you are!

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.610
What's that?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:26.490
Looks like a submarine entrance.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.700
It's visible now because the tide is out.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.990
Maybe we can escape through that hole with our Gratan.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:34.290
Gratan?

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.790
Right! Grandis's Tank, Gratan for short.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.500
It's an all-purpose tank I created.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.710
Unfortunately, it cannot operate underwater.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:46.670
What's wrong with you?

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:48.220
Why did you do that?

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:55.260
Why call it Gratan when I gave it the beautiful name of Katherine?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:59.690
This Gratan... I mean Katherine, where is it?

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.110
It was damaged a bit so we hid it away in the forest.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.440
I don't think they've found it yet.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.030
I see.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:15.410
Hanson! You can fix it right away, can't you? Go bring it here!

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.410
Sure, but... why?

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.920
It's going to be tough, even for the Gratan, I think.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:22.920
Why?

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.130
Look over there.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:29.130
This secret base is heavily guarded.

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:33.140
It won't be easy to get in or out.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.930
Quit complaining! Do something!
You're men, aren't you?

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.430
But what can we do?

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.440
What's that?

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.730
Oh, that's the water intake for the power plant.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.860
What's the water for?

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.150
In a thermoelectric power plant,

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:55.280
they create steam for turning the turbines to generate electricity.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.040
Then, if we cut off that water...

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.540
A blackout!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.550
Magnificent.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.300
Look at these beautiful works of art.

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:18.930
They were all created by the people of Atlantis 12,000 years ago.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.940
They were superior not only in science, but also in the arts.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:30.900
Now, here's something that humans could not hope to duplicate.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.870
Was my discourse on the arts a little difficult for you?

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.990
Sir, I'd like to report.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:44.670
The boy has still not been found. The search is being continued.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.000
And...

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.500
And? What?

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:53.050
I'm sorry, but the three prisoners escaped.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.550
I see. That's okay.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:02.060
Nadia, it's sooner than I thought, but you're going to help us.

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.230
What's his name?

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.520
I'm asking you what your boyfriend's name is.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:18.280
Remember what I told you. Whatever happens, you're responsible.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.990
Can you remember his name?

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.580
Jean...

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:29.000
Jean Rocque Raltique.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.550
Jean Rocque Raltique, can you hear me?

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.060
You'd better give yourself up quietly.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:47.020
That's the only way you can save the lives of Nadia and her friends.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:52.110
I repeat, Jean Rocque Raltique,

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:55.280
give yourself up quietly.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:59.070
That's a dirty trick.

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.910
We don't have much time. Let's hurry!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.620
Right!

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.450
Hey, this is no time for self pity.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:08.040
Let's go.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:19.760
Sanson!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.680
What? This is unbelievable!

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.110
This is

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.740
unbelievable...

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.070
Give me this!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.080
We now have one set of disguises.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.740
That was amazing!

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:48.910
No competition for me.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.380
We need one more set.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:52.670
Right!

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:53.840
Sanson...

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.760
Thanks.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:01.720
You have to learn how to take care of yourself, little boy.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.900
How do you feel?

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.780
Bad, of course!

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.780
I didn't want to go to such extremes.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:29.250
I can't afford to lose any more time.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.790
You must see that.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.540
Forget about me,

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:35.540
but let these two go!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.510
That won't help you, Nadia.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:44.930
When the deadline comes, they'll die one by one.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.260
The more of them there are,

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:49.810
the longer you'll live.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.100
You're not human!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:57.690
Exactly! I'm glad you think of me that way.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.280
Heave, ho... Heave, HO!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.830
That should do it. The cooling water has stopped flowing.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:20.050
Yeah, the boiler will start to overheat in a little while.

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.510
Then, boom!

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.970
Jean Rocque Raltique,

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.850
I'll wait one more hour.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.350
If you don't appear by that time,

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:35.600
the baby lion will say goodbye to this world.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:41.400
Are you ready? We'll start our attack.

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.150
That's a good boy.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.410
Let's go!

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.180
Come in.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.180
Jean Rocque Raltique has given up, Sir.

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.440
I see. Take him to the main hall.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.900
Yes, Sir!

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:21.570
What a brave lad.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.570
Is it love that gives him strength?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:49.220
Welcome, Jean Rocque Raltique.

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:50.640
Where is Nadia?

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:58.600
Jean!

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:05.900
Now, Jean, tell me where the Blue Water is.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:10.320
We know that Nadia gave the Blue Water to you.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.790
It's in exchange for the lives of these three.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.540
I don't think that's a bad deal.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:16.790
Jean, don't tell him!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.040
I won't tell you!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:22.920
How do I know you won't kill us anyway as soon as I tell you?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.420
First send all these soldiers away, and set Nadia and the others free.

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.220
Jean!

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.930
You make sense.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:48.820
Jean, did you have the Blue Water all this time?

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.370
Yes, I'm sorry I mislead you.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.780
Fooled by a little kid.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:56.250
Oh, well, makes no difference now.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:15:00.170
Besides, I don't like these guys!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:04.250
Now, Jean, you'd better start talking.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.210
That's not necessary!

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:09.840
Grandis?

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:13.850
Now, set Nadia free, or else you'll get hurt!

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:16.350
I don't know about that.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.690
I'm pretty good with guns.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.690
Well, why don't you give it a try?

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:22.480
Okay!

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.610
I can't believe it.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.490
I have a shield of special textite around me.

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.740
That gun can't even scratch me.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:47.300
That's being smart.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.800
I'll ask you again. Where is the Blue Water?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.190
What is this?

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.560
The power plant has blown up!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:05.480
What?

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.240
Hanson!

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.240
They have support!

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.240
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.490
Nice timing!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.410
Watch out! Stop! It's dangerous!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.080
Stop firing! You'll only hit each other!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.460
Emergency power will be switched on!

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.250
Good!

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.210
Damn...

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:31.550
Commander!

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.680
H- H- How...

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:40.930
No!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.770
Goodbye! Adios! Sayonara!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:47.110
After them! Don't let them get away!

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:47.560
Yes, Sir!

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.410
Deploy the tracking robot tank! We're going to stop them!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:58.910
Yes, Sir!

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:06.670
Gargoyle may be good, but he won't catch us with me at the wheel!

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.590
Is he always like this?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.720
Let me down!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:17.390
What's that?

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:22.180
So, you want to tangle with me?

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:24.020
Come on! Come on! Come on! Come on!

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:24.940
Take this!

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:30.610
Got you! Get out of my way! Get out of my way!

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:39.780
What?

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.620
All right!

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.160
You won't stop me!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.210
We're going to crash!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.010
Don't worry! All under control!

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:09.940
Please, I can't take any more!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:12.610
What's that?

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.450
Right, one more time!

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:20.870
Damn, damn!

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.660
The lake! Dive into the lake!

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:24.660
Gotcha!

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:30.170
Changing to sailing mode, switch on!

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.930
Let's make our getaway through that hole.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.600
My thoughts exactly.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:45.810
Get out of my way!

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:55.940
Cease all resistance and come to a stop,

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:59.240
or we'll blast you out of the water.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.450
I guess it's the end.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:13.880
We almost made it.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.680
What is that?

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.060
The Nautilus?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.440
What? The Nautilus? How did it get in?

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.230
I'm sorry, Sir.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:35.900
You fool.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.860
Prepare the Tower of Babel for firing. Target, the Nautilus.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.450
But Lord Gargoyle,

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:45.870
our power generator was destroyed. We only have three percent power!

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:50.960
It doesn't matter. Concentrate all power on the Nautilus.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:01.260
Incredible...

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.090
Just in time.

00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.720
Let's get away from the island right now.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:06.970
Yes, Ma'am!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.890
I'm going to get Nadia down.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.360
The Garfish is silent.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.780
Commence the second phase of our attack.

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:24.280
Aye, Sir.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.670
A barrier?

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.380
Exactly...

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.750
All circuits ready.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:37.920
Pressure, normal.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.880
Power output up to three point two percent!

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:43.300
Target Nautilus entrapped.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:44.930
Thrity seconds to firing.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:50.770
This is absurd. You can't use the Tower of Babel.

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:54.770
Farewell, Nemo and the Nautilus.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.730
Emergency dive! Hurry!

00:20:58.230 --> 00:20:59.860
Ten seconds to firing.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:00.650
9...

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:01.650
8...

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:02.940
7...

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:03.900
6...

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:04.950
5...

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:06.360
4...

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:06.950
3...

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:08.950
2...

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:09.870
1...

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:15.230
The base built at enormous cost and over so many years is all gone.

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:19.900
It doesn't matter. It's better than letting Nemo find out our secret.

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:21.820
But...

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:24.730
More importantly, who's responsible

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:28.320
for letting that small group get on the island, and destroy it?

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:29.820
That's...

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:34.200
You have to pay for it with your life.

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:46.380
You foolish human beings.

00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:59.940
Oh yeah! There's something I have to return to you.

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:06.190
Thank you, Jean, for coming, and saving me.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.740
This is the second time.

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:15.740
I'm just glad everyone came through safe and sound.

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:20.870
It didn't turn out so good for us!

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.470
The Nautilus

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:31.930
and

